sequenceDiagram
accTitle: Acceptance and database commit are different events
accDescr: The API acknowledges durable queue intake first. A bounded worker commits an idempotent transaction before successful processing removes the message, and failures can retry safely.
participant C as Client
participant A as API
participant Q as SQS
participant W as Lambda consumer
participant D as PostgreSQL
C->>A: Submit with stable request ID
A->>Q: Persist work item
Q-->>A: Send succeeds
A-->>C: Accepted, processing pending
W->>Q: Event source mapping polls queue
Q-->>W: Deliver work batch
W->>D: Idempotent transaction
D-->>W: Commit succeeds
W-->>Q: Successful processing, mapping deletes message
Note over W,D: Retry after commit uses the same request ID
